; An `any`-content prelude TAG in MEMBER position — `eb64url` (#6.21(any)), standing for its three
; siblings `eb64legacy` (#6.22), `eb16` (#6.23) and `cbor-any` (#6.55799). Each tags an ARBITRARY
; CBOR item with advice ABOUT that item (a self-describe marker, or the base64url/base64/base16
; conversion a consumer should use when rendering it as text), so the payload is `any` and the tag
; constrains nothing a generated type could hold. It is REJECTED GRACEFULLY, in every position, at
; `IntermediateTypes::new_type`'s unresolved-reserved fallback — the one seam every position funnels
; through, which is why the message names the TYPE and its TAG and never the position.
;
; It gets a catalog row rather than riding the message pin alone because the row is what catches a
; regression back to an ABORT: the refusal replaced a `panic!` in `cddl_prelude` that is still
; present as a guard, and a future refactor routing a member around `new_type` would restore the
; abort silently. The rule-body siblings are the `tests/matrix_reject/prelude.*.cddl` rows; the
; message text for all four names is pinned by
; `any_content_prelude_tags_reject_gracefully_in_every_position` (src/tests/robustness_tests.rs).
;
; NOT a widening: `any` is the supported way to carry an arbitrary CBOR item in this position — see
; tests/robustness/any_member.cddl — but it drops the tag and the conversion it advertises, so it is
; a different spec, which is why this stays a refusal.
a = [v: eb64url, x: uint]
